/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributes::changeLineColor(Color target, number seconds, int easing)
\brief Animate stroke color.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineColor() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Target Color, interpolated component by component.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing Integer easing constant, such as \c pdg.linearTween or \c pdg.easeInOutQuad.

\return This object, for chaining.

\note Advance a standalone object with animate(deltaSeconds). Drawing and ElementRef copy a sample of Attributes; use ElementRef.setLiveAttributes() to follow later samples. MVC controllers advance their Views automatically.

\see lineColor(), Animated::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributes::changeLineThickness(number target, number seconds, int easing)
\brief Animate stroke thickness.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineThickness() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Finite target stroke width in drawing/Port units.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing Integer easing constant, such as \c pdg.linearTween or \c pdg.easeInOutQuad.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see lineThickness(), Animated::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributes::changeLineOpacity(number target, number seconds, int easing)
\brief Animate stroke opacity.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate lineOpacity() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Resolves lineStyle_Auto to a solid stroke.

\param target Finite target opacity, normally from 0 to 1.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing Integer easing constant, such as \c pdg.linearTween or \c pdg.easeInOutQuad.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see lineOpacity(), Animated::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributes::changeFillColor(Color target, number seconds, int easing)
\brief Animate solid fill color.

Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait. The immediate fillColor() setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue. Selects a solid fill and replaces previous solid/gradient fill-color tracks. Fill opacity remains independent.

\param target Target Color, interpolated component by component.
\param seconds Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds. Zero applies the target immediately. After wait() or andThen(), duration must be greater than zero.
\param easing Integer easing constant, such as \c pdg.linearTween or \c pdg.easeInOutQuad.

\return This object, for chaining.

\note Advance a standalone object with animate(deltaSeconds). Drawing and ElementRef copy a sample of Attributes; use ElementRef.setLiveAttributes() to follow later samples. MVC controllers advance their Views automatically.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const style = new pdg.AnimatedAttributes();
style.fillColor(new pdg.Color(1, 0, 0));
style.changeFillColor(new pdg.Color(0, 0, 1), 0.5);
style.animate(0.25);
const drawing = pdg.createDrawing();
const element = drawing.addRect(new pdg.Rect(0, 0, 20, 10), style);
style.animate(0.25);
element.setAttributes(style);
\endcode

\see fillColor(), Animated::wait(), animate()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::AnimatedAttributes::changeFillOpacity(number target, number seconds, int easing)
